[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Class 7 Single Segment Low Risk Security Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @vcr_grammar

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document specifies cybersecurity requirements for Class 7 vehicle components: **Single Segment Low Risk**.

Class 7 devices are truck modules connected to a single vehicle network segment found to have a low overall fleet risk.

Examples include:
- Electric Propulsion Control Unit #1
- Retarder Display (J1939 SA 23)
- Shift Console - Secondary (J1939 SA 06)
- Transmission Display - Secondary (J1939 SA 60)
- Chassis Controller #1 / SAM Chassis (J1939 SA 71)
- Passenger-Operator Climate Control #1 / LECM / HVAC (J1939 SA 25)
- Battery Pack Monitor #1 (J1939 SA 243)
- Slope Sensor / Hill Start Assist
- Aftertreatment #1 / #2 system gas outlet / NOx sensors (J1939 SA 82, 87)
- Axle - Steering (J1939 SA 08)
- Steering Column Unit / Turn Signal Control
- Steering Wheel Switches (J1939 SA 77)
- Auxiliary Valve Control / Engine Air System Valve Control (J1939 SA 34)
- Catalyst Fluid Sensor / DEF Quality Sensor (J1939 SA 211)
- Seat Control #1
- Turbocharger, Wastegate, Compressor Bypass (J1939 SA 02)
- Door Controller / Door Controllers #1-#4 (J1939 SA 236, 237)
- Engine Exhaust Gas Recirculation (J1939 SA 70)
- Cab Display #1
- Vehicle Security (J1939 SA 29)
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Baseline Security Requirements Applicability

